      },
      "examples": [
        "¿Con quién piensas ir al cine? (Who are you thinking of going to the cinema with?)",
        "Siempre pienso en mis vacaciones. (I'm always thinking about my vacation.)",
        "Ella sale con un chico de la clase. (She's going out with a guy from class.)",
        "¿Con quién sueñas? (Who do you dream about?)"
      ],
      "aid_note": "Romanian also uses verb+preposition combinations, but the pairings are often different. For example, Romanian 'a gândi LA' (think at) vs Spanish 'pensar EN'. There's no reliable cross-language mapping — each verb+preposition pair must be memorized individually. However, Romanian speakers should note that Spanish prepositions (en, con, a, de) are the same words used in Romanian."
